From 1b44cd2fc3586b70dc3920e9c85ae521583c4afb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:42:49 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] popups: XWayland menus and xdg_popups open where the app
 asked

XWayland: a window-less child (an override-redirect menu with a
WM_TRANSIENT_FOR parent) sits in its parent's container, so its element
position is its root position minus the parent's. The old code subtracted
the child's own previous position as well, which was harmless while X
believed every window was at 0,0, but sent menus far to the bottom-right
(the GParted context menu) once X learned the real window positions. Also
tells X the window's position after it is mapped, so a window placed by
the workspace (zones, cascade) reports correct root coordinates.

xdg_popup: the surface is offset by the popup's window geometry (the
menu's shadow), and the popup is unconstrained to the output it opens on
(wlr_xdg_popup_unconstrain_from_box, in toplevel coordinates), so a menu
near an output edge flips instead of being cut.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
